From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:23:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] canvas: "webgl" is the context name it is, not only in a
 conformant build

GetCanvasContextType mapped "webgl" to WebGL 1 only under MOZ_WEBGL_CONFORMANT,
a mozconfig variable this build never set. getContext("webgl") then answered
null, with no webglcontextcreationerror and whatever the attributes, while
"experimental-webgl" answered a context of the same implementation: a page that
asks only for the standard name had no WebGL, and EaglercraftX 1.8.8 warned that
its context was "experimental" (cavekit-eaglercraft.md R2, T-666; read on the
device with render/goanna/test/jihad-webgl-attrs.html). WebGL 1.0 section 2.1
makes the two names aliases; "webgl" now is one, in every build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MpagfKTnbF5UuSGLUYcN1P
---
 dom/canvas/CanvasUtils.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dom/canvas/CanvasUtils.cpp b/dom/canvas/CanvasUtils.cpp
index c7cfed83f6..9acadc8164 100644
--- a/dom/canvas/CanvasUtils.cpp
+++ b/dom/canvas/CanvasUtils.cpp
@@ -43,7 +43,11 @@ GetCanvasContextType(const nsAString& str, dom::CanvasContextType* const out_typ
     return true;
   }
 
-#ifdef MOZ_WEBGL_CONFORMANT
+  // Jihad: "webgl" always, not only in a build configured MOZ_WEBGL_CONFORMANT (a mozconfig
+  // variable this build never set): without it the standard name answered null, with no
+  // webglcontextcreationerror, while "experimental-webgl" answered a context of the same
+  // implementation; a page asking only for "webgl" had no WebGL at all, and EaglercraftX
+  // warned that its context was "experimental" (cavekit-eaglercraft.md R2, T-666).
   if (str.EqualsLiteral("webgl")) {
     /* WebGL 1.0, $2.1 "Context Creation":
      *   If the user agent supports both the webgl and experimental-webgl
@@ -52,7 +56,6 @@ GetCanvasContextType(const nsAString& str, dom::CanvasContextType* const out_typ
     *out_type = dom::CanvasContextType::WebGL1;
     return true;
   }
-#endif
 
   if (WebGL2Context::IsSupported()) {
     if (str.EqualsLiteral("webgl2")) {
